 "_comment": "Stage 0: tune the baselines' single free parameter (Banditron gamma, LinUCB alpha, CTS/LinTS v; the paper gives none). Seeds 100-101 are disjoint from the evaluation seeds 0-9. 1M rounds with one drift at 500k. Same grid size for every baseline (8 values, spanning 2 orders of magnitude). NeuralBandit uses the paper's values and is not tuned. Then run scripts/select_tuned.py, which writes configs/tuned.json and warns if a winner is at the edge of its grid. For another dataset: --data <name> --set T=400000 period=200000.",
